  "summary": "Traditional Krakow nativity scenes featuring colorful, multi-tiered structures with historical and contemporary architecture.",
  "description": "Szopki are elaborate nativity scenes crafted in the shape of historic Krakow buildings, decorated with colorful paper, foil, and various materials, featuring biblical figures alongside contemporary Polish celebrities and political figures. This folk tradition emerged in the 19th century as a way for craftsmen to supplement their income during the Christmas season, blending religious themes with local architectural elements and social commentary in increasingly elaborate designs.",
